tara-cs: Heads-up: BrightCart started seeing a burst of 429s during onboarding after they switched to ephemeral token exchange from the mobile client. Happened ~09:12 UTC when they hit a traffic spike.

sam-cs: Can you paste the client logs and the HTTP response headers?

tara-cs: Pulled a short extract from their proxy logs: 
```
POST /v1/preflight 429  (x-retry-after: 30)
{"error":"rate_limited","message":"preflight quota exceeded"}
---
client: mobile-sdk-ios v1.4.2
request_id: r_0a9b3c
```

james-eng: That looks like token refresh is happening per-request (no caching). They exchange on every call so the preflight fanouts stack and hit the preflight quota. Retry-After is present which helps but stampede already occurred.

james-eng: Short-term fix: cache the exchanged token for the session (eg 30-60s) and reuse for subsequent calls. Long-term: prefer server-side exchange and issue a session token to the client. Example snippet: 
```js
// server side exchange (pseudo)
app.get('/exchange', async (req,res)=>{
  const svcToken = await exchangeEphemeral(req.body.clientId);
  cache.set(req.session.id, svcToken, 60); // reuse 60s
  res.json({token: svcToken});
});
// client
const token = await fetch('/exchange');
fetch(api, {headers:{Authorization:`Bearer ${token}`}});
```

sam-cs: Can we also recommend jitter/backoff on the client preflight to avoid synchronized retries? :thinking: 

james-eng: Yes. Configure client preflight jitter (200-800ms) + exponential backoff (factor 1.5, max ~5s) and limit preflight concurrency per device. Also enable SDK option prefetch: true to coalesce initial requests.

leo-sre: We can temporarily open a per-org burst window for BrightCart while they patch. I can bump their preflight burst multiplier to 3x for 60 minutes. Need org_id and region here.

tara-cs: org_id=brightcart-prod-22, region=us-west-2. I notified their eng lead and they're shipping a quick cache patch now.

ratebot: :rotating_light: Policy update executed by leo-sre — per-org burst increase applied for brightcart-prod-22, expires in 60m. Change-id: policy-2026-09-12-0007

tara-cs: Quick update — they shipped token-cache and turned on jitter. 429s dropped from ~80/min to single digits within 10m. Monitoring in progress.

sam-cs: Awesome. Can you add a short onboarding checklist item/PR on GH so future accounts avoid this? Link to the SDK flags would be great.

tara-cs: Will open PR to docs and ping eng docs channel. Also adding a short note to our onboarding runbook about requesting temporary burst increases.

james-eng: I'll add a recommended config block to the SDK README and the sample app.

tara-cs: Thanks all — closing the immediate incident. Will follow up with a one-pager for CSMs and a post-onboard retro. :rocket:
